{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwRGFQG92mRjcVfRnuCfuj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! The starter game, and the template for a new one: collect every shard while slimes chase\n2\t//! you round the walls. Three lives; a slime's touch sends everyone back to the start.\n3\t//!\n4\t//! To start a game of your own, copy this file and `starter.toml` to `<key>.rs` and\n5\t//! `<key>.toml`, change `KEY`, add its line to `GAMES` in `mod.rs`, then change the rules.\n6\t//! `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` walks through it.\n7\t\n8\tuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\n9\tuse std::sync::Arc;\n10\t\n11\tuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\n12\tuse glam::{Vec2, Vec3};\n13\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n14\tuse serde_json::json;\n15\t\n16\tuse super::{Game, GameBox, Outcome};\n17\tuse crate::color::Color;\n18\tuse crate::entity::{Behavior, EntityId, Spawn};\n19\tuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\n20\tuse crate::input::InputFrame;\n21\tuse crate::nav::NavGrid;\n22\tuse crate::room::RoomDef;\n23\tuse crate::shape::{Shape, Visual};\n24\tuse crate::sim::Sim;\n25\t\n26\t/// The level, a room file, built in (the browser has no files). Running from the repository,\n27\t/// `level_text` reads the file on disk instead, so an edit shows at the next `load`.\n28\tconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\"starter.toml\");\n29\t\n30\t/// The rules' numbers: the level's `[game]` table, each with a default, so balancing is an\n31\t/// edit to the level and a `load` (no rebuild).\n32\t#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n33\t#[serde(default, deny_unknown_fields)]\n34\tpub struct Rules {\n35\t    pub lives: u32,\n36\t    /// Slime speed as a fraction of a walker's top speed (each slime gets ±15%, from the seed).\n37\t    pub slime_speed: f32,\n38\t    /// Slimes chase a player within this walking distance (m).\n39\t    pub slime_sight: f32,\n40\t    /// Feet closer than this (m) catch the player.\n41\t    pub catch: f32,\n42\t    /// Feet closer than this (m) to a shard pick it up.\n43\t    pub pick: f32,\n44\t    /// Seconds the player is safe at the start and after a catch.\n45\t    pub grace: f32,\n46\t}\n47\t\n48\timpl Default for Rules {\n49\t    fn default() -> Self {\n50\t        Self { lives: 3, slime_speed: 0.5, slime_sight: 9.0, catch: 0.8, pick: 0.9, grace: 2.0 }\n51\t    }\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\t#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n55\tpub struct Starter {\n56\t    pub rules: Rules,\n57\t    /// Shards still on the floor.\n58\t    pub shards: Vec<EntityId>,\n59\t    pub total: usize,\n60\t    pub slimes: Vec<EntityId>,\n61\t    /// Each slime's start (feet) and speed.\n62\t    pub homes: Vec<Vec3>,\n63\t    pub speeds: Vec<f32>,\n64\t    pub lives: u32,\n65\t    /// Seconds the player is still safe from slimes.\n66\t    pub grace: f32,\n67\t    pub time: f32,\n68\t    pub outcome: Outcome,\n69\t    /// The walkable grid. It follows from the level alone, so it isn't saved: rebuilt when\n70\t    /// missing (after a snapshot load).\n71\t    #[serde(skip)]\n72\t    nav: Option<Arc<NavGrid>>,\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\t/// Builds the level, places the shards on its `shard` markers and starts the game.\n76\tpub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\n77\t    let def = RoomDef::parse(&super::level_text(Starter::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|e| anyhow!(\"starter.toml: {e}\"))?;\n78\t    let rules: Rules = toml::Value::Table(def.game.clone()).try_into().map_err(|e| anyhow!(\"starter.toml [game]: {e}\"))?;\n79\t    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, Starter::KEY, def);\n80\t    let mut shards = Vec::new();\n81\t    for at in crate::scenes::markers(sim, \"shard\") {\n82\t        let mut look = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::splat(0.2) }, Color::hex(\"#7fe3ff\"));\n83\t        look.emissive = 0.8;\n84\t        let shard = Spawn::new(\"shard\", at + Vec3::Y * 0.7).visual(look).behavior(Behavior::Spin { speed: 2.5 });\n85\t        shards.push(sim.spawn(shard));\n86\t    }\n87\t    // Slimes come from the level's [[npc]] entries; the game drives them.\n88\t    let slimes: Vec<EntityId> = sim.state.entities.iter().filter(|e| e.name == \"slime\").map(|e| e.id).collect();\n89\t    let homes = slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.feet(id)).collect();\n90\t    // Randomness comes from the sim's seeded generator, so a seed always plays the same.\n91\t    let speeds = slimes.iter().map(|_| rules.slime_speed * sim.state.rng.range(0.85, 1.15)).collect();\n92\t    let game = Starter {\n93\t        total: shards.len(),\n94\t        shards,\n95\t        slimes,\n96\t        homes,\n97\t        speeds,\n98\t        lives: rules.lives,\n99\t        grace: rules.grace,\n100\t        rules,\n101\t        time: 0.0,\n102\t        outcome: Outcome::Playing,\n103\t        nav: None,\n104\t    };\n105\t    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(game));\n106\t    Ok(())\n107\t}\n108\t\n109\timpl Game for Starter {\n110\t    const KEY: &'static str = \"starter\";\n111\t\n112\t    fn pre(\n113\t        &mut self,\n114\t        sim: &mut Sim,\n115\t        _input: &InputFrame,\n116\t        _dt: f32,\n117\t        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\n118\t    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\n119\t        let mut out = BTreeMap::new();\n120\t        if self.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\n121\t            // Decided: everyone stands still.\n122\t            for &id in sim.state.player.iter().chain(&self.slimes) {\n123\t                out.insert(id, InputFrame::default());\n124\t            }\n125\t            return out;\n126\t        }\n127\t        if self.nav.is_none() {\n128\t            self.nav = NavGrid::for_room(sim).map(Arc::new);\n129\t        }\n130\t        let Some(nav) = self.nav.clone() else { return out };\n131\t        // One flow field toward the player steers every slime round the walls.\n132\t        let player = sim.state.player.and_then(|id| sim.feet(id));\n133\t        let field = player.filter(|_| self.grace <= 0.0).and_then(|p| nav.flow(p, self.rules.slime_sight));\n134\t        for (&id, &speed) in self.slimes.iter().zip(&self.speeds) {\n135\t            let mut input = InputFrame::default();\n136\t            if let (Some(field), Some(at)) = (&field, sim.feet(id))\n137\t                && let Some(d) = field.dir(&nav, at)\n138\t            {\n139\t                input.move_dir = Vec2::new(d.x, d.z) * speed;\n140\t            }\n141\t            out.insert(id, input);\n142\t        }\n143\t        out\n144\t    }\n145\t\n146\t    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\n147\t        if self.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\n148\t            return;\n149\t        }\n150\t        self.time += dt;\n151\t        self.grace = (self.grace - dt).max(0.0);\n152\t        let Some(pid) = sim.state.player else { return };\n153\t        let Some(p) = sim.feet(pid) else { return };\n154\t\n155\t        // Shards: walk over one to pick it up.\n156\t        let near: Vec<(EntityId, Vec3)> = self\n157\t            .shards\n158\t            .iter()\n159\t            .filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id).map(|e| (id, e.pos)))\n160\t            .filter(|(_, at)| flat(*at - p) < self.rules.pick)\n161\t            .collect();\n162\t        for (id, at) in near {\n163\t            self.shards.retain(|&s| s != id);\n164\t            sim.despawn(id);\n165\t            events.push(SimEvent::Coin { pos: at });\n166\t            let left = self.shards.len();\n167\t            sim.say(if left == 1 { \"1 shard to go\".to_string() } else { format!(\"{left} shards to go\") });\n168\t        }\n169\t        if self.shards.is_empty() {\n170\t            self.outcome = Outcome::Won;\n171\t            sim.say(format!(\"All shards in {:.1} s!\", self.time));\n172\t            return;\n173\t        }\n174\t\n175\t        // Slimes: a touch costs a life and sends everyone back to the start.\n176\t        let catch = self.rules.catch;\n177\t        let caught = self.grace <= 0.0 && self.slimes.iter().any(|&id| sim.feet(id).is_some_and(|s| flat(s - p) < catch));\n178\t        if caught {\n179\t            self.lives -= 1;\n180\t            events.push(SimEvent::Hit { pos: p + Vec3::Y, strength: 1.0, target: Some(pid) });\n181\t            if self.lives == 0 {\n182\t                self.outcome = Outcome::Lost;\n183\t                sim.say(\"Caught! Game over\");\n184\t                return;\n185\t            }\n186\t            sim.say(format!(\"Caught! {} lives left\", self.lives));\n187\t            let spawn = sim.state.spawn;\n188\t            sim.set_position(pid, spawn);\n189\t            for (&id, &home) in self.slimes.iter().zip(&self.homes) {\n190\t                sim.set_position(id, home);\n191\t            }\n192\t            self.grace = self.rules.grace;\n193\t        }\n194\t    }\n195\t\n196\t    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\n197\t        let mut lines =\n198\t            vec![format!(\"Shards {}/{}\", self.total - self.shards.len(), self.total), format!(\"Lives {}\", self.lives)];\n199\t        match self.outcome {\n200\t            Outcome::Won => lines.push(format!(\"You win! {:.1} s\", self.time)),\n201\t            Outcome::Lost => lines.push(\"Game over\".into()),\n202\t            Outcome::Playing => {}\n203\t        }\n204\t        lines\n205\t    }\n206\t\n207\t    fn status(&self, sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\n208\t        let xz = |id: EntityId| sim.feet(id).map(|f| [round(f.x), round(f.z)]);\n209\t        json!({\n210\t            \"outcome\": self.outcome,\n211\t            \"time\": round(self.time),\n212\t            \"shards_left\": self.shards.len(),\n213\t            \"total\": self.total,\n214\t            \"lives\": self.lives,\n215\t            \"grace\": round(self.grace),\n216\t            \"player\": sim.state.player.and_then(xz),\n217\t            \"shards\": self.shards.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id).map(|e| [round(e.pos.x), round(e.pos.z)])).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n218\t            \"slimes\": self.slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| xz(id)).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n219\t        })\n220\t    }\n221\t\n222\t    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\n223\t        self.outcome\n224\t    }\n225\t\n226\t    /// Takes the shortest walk to a shard that keeps clear of slimes (cells near them count\n227\t    /// as walls); with every shard cut off, makes for the reachable spot farthest from them.\n228\t    fn bot(&self, sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\n229\t        let mut input = InputFrame::default();\n230\t        let Some(p) = sim.state.player.and_then(|id| sim.feet(id)) else { return input };\n231\t        let Some(mut grid) = self.nav.as_deref().cloned().or_else(|| NavGrid::for_room(sim)) else { return input };\n232\t        let slimes: Vec<Vec3> = self.slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.feet(id)).collect();\n233\t        if self.grace < 0.5 {\n234\t            for i in 0..grid.blocked.len() {\n235\t                if slimes.iter().any(|&s| flat(grid.center(i) - s) < 1.8) {\n236\t                    grid.blocked[i] = true;\n237\t                }\n238\t            }\n239\t        }\n240\t        let paths = self.shards.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id)).filter_map(|e| grid.path(p, e.pos));\n241\t        let path = paths.min_by(|a, b| length(p, a).total_cmp(&length(p, b))).or_else(|| {\n242\t            let clearance = |i: usize| slimes.iter().map(|&s| flat(grid.center(i) - s)).fold(f32::MAX, f32::min);\n243\t            let reach = grid.flow(p, 6.0)?;\n244\t            let safest = (0..grid.blocked.len())\n245\t                .filter(|&i| reach.dist[i].is_finite())\n246\t                .max_by(|&a, &b| clearance(a).total_cmp(&clearance(b)))?;\n247\t            grid.path(p, grid.center(safest))\n248\t        });\n249\t        input.move_dir = path.map(|path| flat_dir(path[0] - p)).unwrap_or_default();\n250\t        input\n251\t    }\n252\t}\n253\t\n254\tfn flat(v: Vec3) -> f32 {\n255\t    Vec2::new(v.x, v.z).length()\n256\t}\n257\t\n258\tfn flat_dir(v: Vec3) -> Vec2 {\n259\t    Vec2::new(v.x, v.z).normalize_or_zero()\n260\t}\n261\t\n262\t/// Walking length of a path from `p`.\n263\tfn length(p: Vec3, path: &[Vec3]) -> f32 {\n264\t    let (mut at, mut sum) = (p, 0.0);\n265\t    for &q in path {\n266\t        sum += flat(q - at);\n267\t        at = q;\n268\t    }\n269\t    sum\n270\t}\n271\t\n272\tfn round(x: f32) -> f64 {\n273\t    (x as f64 * 100.0).round() / 100.0\n274\t}\n275\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3d8a44-de88-4121-ac6f-adf7ca0c1ca2","uuid":"e3a4c216-ef4b-4cb9-820d-58b379f88a53","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:48.599Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work/.research/shardfall/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs","content":"//! The starter game, and the template for a new one: collect every shard while slimes chase\n//! you round the walls. Three lives; a slime's touch sends everyone back to the start.\n//!\n//! To start a game of your own, copy this file and `starter.toml` to `<key>.rs` and\n//! `<key>.toml`, change `KEY`, add its line to `GAMES` in `mod.rs`, then change the rules.\n//! `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` walks through it.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\nuse glam::{Vec2, Vec3};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse serde_json::json;\n\nuse super::{Game, GameBox, Outcome};\nuse crate::color::Color;\nuse crate::entity::{Behavior, EntityId, Spawn};\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\nuse crate::nav::NavGrid;\nuse crate::room::RoomDef;\nuse crate::shape::{Shape, Visual};\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\n\n/// The level, a room file, built in (the browser has no files). Running from the repository,\n/// `level_text` reads the file on disk instead, so an edit shows at the next `load`.\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\"starter.toml\");\n\n/// The rules' numbers: the level's `[game]` table, each with a default, so balancing is an\n/// edit to the level and a `load` (no rebuild).\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(default, deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct Rules {\n    pub lives: u32,\n    /// Slime speed as a fraction of a walker's top speed (each slime gets ±15%, from the seed).\n    pub slime_speed: f32,\n    /// Slimes chase a player within this walking distance (m).\n    pub slime_sight: f32,\n    /// Feet closer than this (m) catch the player.\n    pub catch: f32,\n    /// Feet closer than this (m) to a shard pick it up.\n    pub pick: f32,\n    /// Seconds the player is safe at the start and after a catch.\n    pub grace: f32,\n}\n\nimpl Default for Rules {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self { lives: 3, slime_speed: 0.5, slime_sight: 9.0, catch: 0.8, pick: 0.9, grace: 2.0 }\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct Starter {\n    pub rules: Rules,\n    /// Shards still on the floor.\n    pub shards: Vec<EntityId>,\n    pub total: usize,\n    pub slimes: Vec<EntityId>,\n    /// Each slime's start (feet) and speed.\n    pub homes: Vec<Vec3>,\n    pub speeds: Vec<f32>,\n    pub lives: u32,\n    /// Seconds the player is still safe from slimes.\n    pub grace: f32,\n    pub time: f32,\n    pub outcome: Outcome,\n    /// The walkable grid. It follows from the level alone, so it isn't saved: rebuilt when\n    /// missing (after a snapshot load).\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    nav: Option<Arc<NavGrid>>,\n}\n\n/// Builds the level, places the shards on its `shard` markers and starts the game.\npub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\n    let def = RoomDef::parse(&super::level_text(Starter::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|e| anyhow!(\"starter.toml: {e}\"))?;\n    let rules: Rules = toml::Value::Table(def.game.clone()).try_into().map_err(|e| anyhow!(\"starter.toml [game]: {e}\"))?;\n    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, Starter::KEY, def);\n    let mut shards = Vec::new();\n    for at in crate::scenes::markers(sim, \"shard\") {\n        let mut look = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::splat(0.2) }, Color::hex(\"#7fe3ff\"));\n        look.emissive = 0.8;\n        let shard = Spawn::new(\"shard\", at + Vec3::Y * 0.7).visual(look).behavior(Behavior::Spin { speed: 2.5 });\n        shards.push(sim.spawn(shard));\n    }\n    // Slimes come from the level's [[npc]] entries; the game drives them.\n    let slimes: Vec<EntityId> = sim.state.entities.iter().filter(|e| e.name == \"slime\").map(|e| e.id).collect();\n    let homes = slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.feet(id)).collect();\n    // Randomness comes from the sim's seeded generator, so a seed always plays the same.\n    let speeds = slimes.iter().map(|_| rules.slime_speed * sim.state.rng.range(0.85, 1.15)).collect();\n    let game = Starter {\n        total: shards.len(),\n        shards,\n        slimes,\n        homes,\n        speeds,\n        lives: rules.lives,\n        grace: rules.grace,\n        rules,\n        time: 0.0,\n        outcome: Outcome::Playing,\n        nav: None,\n    };\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(game));\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nimpl Game for Starter {\n    const KEY: &'static str = \"starter\";\n\n    fn pre(\n        &mut self,\n        sim: &mut Sim,\n        _input: &InputFrame,\n        _dt: f32,\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\n        let mut out = BTreeMap::new();\n        if self.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\n            // Decided: everyone stands still.\n            for &id in sim.state.player.iter().chain(&self.slimes) {\n                out.insert(id, InputFrame::default());\n            }\n            return out;\n        }\n        if self.nav.is_none() {\n            self.nav = NavGrid::for_room(sim).map(Arc::new);\n        }\n        let Some(nav) = self.nav.clone() else { return out };\n        // One flow field toward the player steers every slime round the walls.\n        let player = sim.state.player.and_then(|id| sim.feet(id));\n        let field = player.filter(|_| self.grace <= 0.0).and_then(|p| nav.flow(p, self.rules.slime_sight));\n        for (&id, &speed) in self.slimes.iter().zip(&self.speeds) {\n            let mut input = InputFrame::default();\n            if let (Some(field), Some(at)) = (&field, sim.feet(id))\n                && let Some(d) = field.dir(&nav, at)\n            {\n                input.move_dir = Vec2::new(d.x, d.z) * speed;\n            }\n            out.insert(id, input);\n        }\n        out\n    }\n\n    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\n        if self.outcome != Outcome::Playing {\n            return;\n        }\n        self.time += dt;\n        self.grace = (self.grace - dt).max(0.0);\n        let Some(pid) = sim.state.player else { return };\n        let Some(p) = sim.feet(pid) else { return };\n\n        // Shards: walk over one to pick it up.\n        let near: Vec<(EntityId, Vec3)> = self\n            .shards\n            .iter()\n            .filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id).map(|e| (id, e.pos)))\n            .filter(|(_, at)| flat(*at - p) < self.rules.pick)\n            .collect();\n        for (id, at) in near {\n            self.shards.retain(|&s| s != id);\n            sim.despawn(id);\n            events.push(SimEvent::Coin { pos: at });\n            let left = self.shards.len();\n            sim.say(if left == 1 { \"1 shard to go\".to_string() } else { format!(\"{left} shards to go\") });\n        }\n        if self.shards.is_empty() {\n            self.outcome = Outcome::Won;\n            sim.say(format!(\"All shards in {:.1} s!\", self.time));\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Slimes: a touch costs a life and sends everyone back to the start.\n        let catch = self.rules.catch;\n        let caught = self.grace <= 0.0 && self.slimes.iter().any(|&id| sim.feet(id).is_some_and(|s| flat(s - p) < catch));\n        if caught {\n            self.lives -= 1;\n            events.push(SimEvent::Hit { pos: p + Vec3::Y, strength: 1.0, target: Some(pid) });\n            if self.lives == 0 {\n                self.outcome = Outcome::Lost;\n                sim.say(\"Caught! Game over\");\n                return;\n            }\n            sim.say(format!(\"Caught! {} lives left\", self.lives));\n            let spawn = sim.state.spawn;\n            sim.set_position(pid, spawn);\n            for (&id, &home) in self.slimes.iter().zip(&self.homes) {\n                sim.set_position(id, home);\n            }\n            self.grace = self.rules.grace;\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\n        let mut lines =\n            vec![format!(\"Shards {}/{}\", self.total - self.shards.len(), self.total), format!(\"Lives {}\", self.lives)];\n        match self.outcome {\n            Outcome::Won => lines.push(format!(\"You win! {:.1} s\", self.time)),\n            Outcome::Lost => lines.push(\"Game over\".into()),\n            Outcome::Playing => {}\n        }\n        lines\n    }\n\n    fn status(&self, sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\n        let xz = |id: EntityId| sim.feet(id).map(|f| [round(f.x), round(f.z)]);\n        json!({\n            \"outcome\": self.outcome,\n            \"time\": round(self.time),\n            \"shards_left\": self.shards.len(),\n            \"total\": self.total,\n            \"lives\": self.lives,\n            \"grace\": round(self.grace),\n            \"player\": sim.state.player.and_then(xz),\n            \"shards\": self.shards.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id).map(|e| [round(e.pos.x), round(e.pos.z)])).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n            \"slimes\": self.slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| xz(id)).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\n        self.outcome\n    }\n\n    /// Takes the shortest walk to a shard that keeps clear of slimes (cells near them count\n    /// as walls); with every shard cut off, makes for the reachable spot farthest from them.\n    fn bot(&self, sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\n        let mut input = InputFrame::default();\n        let Some(p) = sim.state.player.and_then(|id| sim.feet(id)) else { return input };\n        let Some(mut grid) = self.nav.as_deref().cloned().or_else(|| NavGrid::for_room(sim)) else { return input };\n        let slimes: Vec<Vec3> = self.slimes.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.feet(id)).collect();\n        if self.grace < 0.5 {\n            for i in 0..grid.blocked.len() {\n                if slimes.iter().any(|&s| flat(grid.center(i) - s) < 1.8) {\n                    grid.blocked[i] = true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        let paths = self.shards.iter().filter_map(|&id| sim.state.entities.get(id)).filter_map(|e| grid.path(p, e.pos));\n        let path = paths.min_by(|a, b| length(p, a).total_cmp(&length(p, b))).or_else(|| {\n            let clearance = |i: usize| slimes.iter().map(|&s| flat(grid.center(i) - s)).fold(f32::MAX, f32::min);\n            let reach = grid.flow(p, 6.0)?;\n            let safest = (0..grid.blocked.len())\n                .filter(|&i| reach.dist[i].is_finite())\n                .max_by(|&a, &b| clearance(a).total_cmp(&clearance(b)))?;\n            grid.path(p, grid.center(safest))\n        });\n        input.move_dir = path.map(|path| flat_dir(path[0] - p)).unwrap_or_default();\n        input\n    }\n}\n\nfn flat(v: Vec3) -> f32 {\n    Vec2::new(v.x, v.z).length()\n}\n\nfn flat_dir(v: Vec3) -> Vec2 {\n    Vec2::new(v.x, v.z).normalize_or_zero()\n}\n\n/// Walking length of a path from `p`.\nfn length(p: Vec3, path: &[Vec3]) -> f32 {\n    let (mut at, mut sum) = (p, 0.0);\n    for &q in path {\n        sum += flat(q - at);\n        at = q;\n    }\n    sum\n}\n\nfn round(x: f32) -> f64 {\n    (x as f64 * 100.0).round() / 100.0\n}\n","numLines":275,"startLine":1,"totalLines":275}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SwRGFQG92mRjcVfRnuCfuj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj95LW4ry49AESbMjKJd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017N2dhBv5L5MH4zFLxdFSWf","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work/.research/shardfall/docs/FEEDBACK.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4462,"cache_read_input_tokens":60749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4462},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3d8a44-de88-4121-ac6f-adf7ca0c1ca2","uuid":"0b2bb2df-b426-421c-a28d-1c56f0bcfa4a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:49.637Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj95LDSxXTBqXfRVkyDr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017N2dhBv5L5MH4zFLxdFSWf":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work/.research/shardfall/docs/FEEDBACK.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017N2dhBv5L5MH4zFLxdFSWf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test-game feedback\n2\t\n3\tEngine feedback from test games: a fresh agent builds a vertical slice of a 1985-2015 classic on\n4\tthis engine, then evaluates the engine. Each game is stored as one self-contained HTML file in\n5\t`michaelcrosato/ai-hub` (`games/`, source zip in `sources/`). The maintainer checks each claim\n6\tagainst the code, fixes what blocks the next game, and waits for patterns before larger work:\n7\tfeatures everyone uses, features no one uses, problems that keep coming back. Newest game first\n8\tunder \"Games\"; the tally is updated with every game.\n9\t\n10\t**Prompt.** The user's template, with the game's name, year and platforms as SOURCE: build an\n11\toriginal spiritual successor as one complete, polished level that doubles as a tech demo; use the\n12\tengine, extend it as needed; deliver one self-contained HTML file; then a one-page candid\n13\tevaluation of the engine (used/not used, engine work you wrote ranked by output saved, engine\n14\tchanges, bugs and wrong docs, source you had to read, fidelity limits, testing, what helped and\n15\thurt, missing features by impact, the one change). The questions get adjusted as patterns show. Since 2026-10-16 the agent starts from\n16\t`START_HERE.md`'s \"Make a game\" prompt: `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` and the starter game, ending with\n17\tthe guide's engine feedback section, which feeds this log.\n18\t\n19\t**Asset store lines** (the store's S3, 2026-10-15; the user pastes them into the template). Each\n20\tgame's answers count toward the store's critical mass (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §13): a need\n21\tis met when the game placed, forked or derived a store entry instead of making it from scratch.\n22\t1. Before you make a prop, material or clip, `assets shelf=prop` (or `shelf=clip`) lists the\n23\t   engine's asset store and `assets find=words` searches it (`store/README.md`).\n24\t2. Assets you looked for: one line each, the query and the id you used, or `none`.\n25\t3. Up to 5 things you built that another game could reuse: the file and one line each.\n26\t\n27\tThe user flags the store entries each game used on a per-game review page (`scripts/\n28\treview_page.py` with a `flags` manifest): looks, feels, reads, works or broken (§7).\n29\t\n30\t**Cost** is counted end to end from the agent's transcript (model calls, tokens read, weighted\n31\tcost at cache reads 0.1, cache writes 1.25, visible output 5; hidden reasoning is not recorded).\n32\t\n33\t## Tally (1 game)\n34\t| Asked for | Games | Impact | Status |\n35\t|---|---|---|---|\n36\t| A supported second-game path: a `Game` hook for step, frame, view and HUD instead of editing `sim.rs`, `frame.rs`, `build.rs` and `app.rs` | 1 | high | **done** (2026-10-16): `pav_core::games` (step, HUD text, status, bot), the starter game, `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`; drawing and HUD widgets still mean view or app code |\n37\t| Entities, shots, health and AI that don't require rapier (`health.rs`, `projectile.rs`) | 1 | high | waiting |\n38\t| A single-file web build (gzip + inline) | 1 | high | **done**: `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file` |\n39\t| Primitive-part models drawn per frame from game state (props can't be) | 1 | medium | **done**: `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` (plan row 4.1) |\n40\t| Stock HUD widgets (bars, radar, off-screen markers, boss bar, banner) | 1 | medium | waiting |\n41\t| Data-driven sound bank (`pav_audio::sounds_for` is a closed match) | 1 | medium | waiting |\n42\t| Per-scene default camera on `load` | 1 | medium | waiting |\n43\t| HUD visible to headless capture | 1 | medium | **done** (2026-10-19): captures draw the game UI (a hook game's HUD lines too); `ui` reads it as text |\n44\t| Open top-down map data (roads, water, spawns) | 1 | low | waiting |\n45\t| Continuous-play and top-down map captures | 1 | low | waiting |\n46\t\n47\t| Engine part | Used | Skipped |\n48\t|---|---|---|\n49\t| `Sim` (rewind, `state_hash`, snapshot), `pav_render::Scene`, particle presets, `pav_audio` synth, `pav_tools` capture/repl/input, the wasm shell and egui, `Rng`/`InputFrame`/bindings | 1 | 0 |\n50\t| rapier entities, `character.rs`, `nav.rs`, `health.rs`, `projectile.rs`, `vehicle.rs` helicopter, `course.rs`, `zones.rs`, `stealth.rs`, `ai.rs` | 0 | 1 |\n51\t| Rooms/TOML, puppet, moves, clips, the asset and creature studios (props, format 2) | 0 | 1 |\n52\t\n53\t## Games\n54\t\n55\t### Capital Strike, from Jungle Strike (1993; SNES, Genesis) — 2026-10-12\n56\t- **Result:** one mission over Washington. Gun, rockets, homing missiles, flares and a dash;\n57\t  armour, fuel and ammo; winch rescues; a motorcade escort; SAMs, AA guns, tanks, gunships and a\n58\t  three-phase boss; loadouts, difficulties, checkpoints, radar and a procedural soundtrack.\n59\t  `ai-hub/games/Jungle-Strike-Capital-Strike-2026-10-12-model-unknown.html` (9.8 MB); source as a\n60\t  patch series against `6618522` in `ai-hub/sources/`.\n61\t- **Agent:** Sonnet at medium effort, a subagent in its own worktree of this repo.\n62\t- **Cost:** 1.65 h, 170 model calls, 54M tokens read (context grew from 56k to 485k), about 6.5M\n63\t  weighted; 106k tokens of visible output. About 4,270 lines written, 3,965 of them game code\n64\t  inside the engine crates.\n65\t- **Verdict (agent's):** the renderer, wasm shell, audio synth and headless tools carried the\n66\t  visuals and the first wasm build ran; the gameplay half didn't help a non-RPG, non-physics game,\n67\t  so 4,000 lines went into a game layer with no engine facility, and the packaging was all its own.\n68\t- **Checked:** the claims about `vehicle.rs` and `health.rs` hold (rapier-bound; no weapons,\n69\t  damage or fuel), and AGENTS.md now says so. The game didn't touch props, format 2 or the studios:\n70\t  its units are SDF and cube parts drawn in code, because a prop can't be drawn from game state.\n71\t- **Acted on:** the single-file web build (every test game needs one), the AGENTS.md wording, and\n72\t  the asset plan's row 4.1 now includes drawing a library asset from game code. Everything else\n73\t  waits for a second game.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3d8a44-de88-4121-ac6f-adf7ca0c1ca2","uuid":"976661a2-cb0f-4204-964f-50d0d503273a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:49.647Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work/.research/shardfall/docs/FEEDBACK.md","content":"# Test-game feedback\n\nEngine feedback from test games: a fresh agent builds a vertical slice of a 1985-2015 classic on\nthis engine, then evaluates the engine. Each game is stored as one self-contained HTML file in\n`michaelcrosato/ai-hub` (`games/`, source zip in `sources/`). The maintainer checks each claim\nagainst the code, fixes what blocks the next game, and waits for patterns before larger work:\nfeatures everyone uses, features no one uses, problems that keep coming back. Newest game first\nunder \"Games\"; the tally is updated with every game.\n\n**Prompt.** The user's template, with the game's name, year and platforms as SOURCE: build an\noriginal spiritual successor as one complete, polished level that doubles as a tech demo; use the\nengine, extend it as needed; deliver one self-contained HTML file; then a one-page candid\nevaluation of the engine (used/not used, engine work you wrote ranked by output saved, engine\nchanges, bugs and wrong docs, source you had to read, fidelity limits, testing, what helped and\nhurt, missing features by impact, the one change). The questions get adjusted as patterns show. Since 2026-10-16 the agent starts from\n`START_HERE.md`'s \"Make a game\" prompt: `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` and the starter game, ending with\nthe guide's engine feedback section, which feeds this log.\n\n**Asset store lines** (the store's S3, 2026-10-15; the user pastes them into the template). Each\ngame's answers count toward the store's critical mass (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §13): a need\nis met when the game placed, forked or derived a store entry instead of making it from scratch.\n1. Before you make a prop, material or clip, `assets shelf=prop` (or `shelf=clip`) lists the\n   engine's asset store and `assets find=words` searches it (`store/README.md`).\n2. Assets you looked for: one line each, the query and the id you used, or `none`.\n3. Up to 5 things you built that another game could reuse: the file and one line each.\n\nThe user flags the store entries each game used on a per-game review page (`scripts/\nreview_page.py` with a `flags` manifest): looks, feels, reads, works or broken (§7).\n\n**Cost** is counted end to end from the agent's transcript (model calls, tokens read, weighted\ncost at cache reads 0.1, cache writes 1.25, visible output 5; hidden reasoning is not recorded).\n\n## Tally (1 game)\n| Asked for | Games | Impact | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A supported second-game path: a `Game` hook for step, frame, view and HUD instead of editing `sim.rs`, `frame.rs`, `build.rs` and `app.rs` | 1 | high | **done** (2026-10-16): `pav_core::games` (step, HUD text, status, bot), the starter game, `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`; drawing and HUD widgets still mean view or app code |\n| Entities, shots, health and AI that don't require rapier (`health.rs`, `projectile.rs`) | 1 | high | waiting |\n| A single-file web build (gzip + inline) | 1 | high | **done**: `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file` |\n| Primitive-part models drawn per frame from game state (props can't be) | 1 | medium | **done**: `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` (plan row 4.1) |\n| Stock HUD widgets (bars, radar, off-screen markers, boss bar, banner) | 1 | medium | waiting |\n| Data-driven sound bank (`pav_audio::sounds_for` is a closed match) | 1 | medium | waiting |\n| Per-scene default camera on `load` | 1 | medium | waiting |\n| HUD visible to headless capture | 1 | medium | **done** (2026-10-19): captures draw the game UI (a hook game's HUD lines too); `ui` reads it as text |\n| Open top-down map data (roads, water, spawns) | 1 | low | waiting |\n| Continuous-play and top-down map captures | 1 | low | waiting |\n\n| Engine part | Used | Skipped |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Sim` (rewind, `state_hash`, snapshot), `pav_render::Scene`, particle presets, `pav_audio` synth, `pav_tools` capture/repl/input, the wasm shell and egui, `Rng`/`InputFrame`/bindings | 1 | 0 |\n| rapier entities, `character.rs`, `nav.rs`, `health.rs`, `projectile.rs`, `vehicle.rs` helicopter, `course.rs`, `zones.rs`, `stealth.rs`, `ai.rs` | 0 | 1 |\n| Rooms/TOML, puppet, moves, clips, the asset and creature studios (props, format 2) | 0 | 1 |\n\n## Games\n\n### Capital Strike, from Jungle Strike (1993; SNES, Genesis) — 2026-10-12\n- **Result:** one mission over Washington. Gun, rockets, homing missiles, flares and a dash;\n  armour, fuel and ammo; winch rescues; a motorcade escort; SAMs, AA guns, tanks, gunships and a\n  three-phase boss; loadouts, difficulties, checkpoints, radar and a procedural soundtrack.\n  `ai-hub/games/Jungle-Strike-Capital-Strike-2026-10-12-model-unknown.html` (9.8 MB); source as a\n  patch series against `6618522` in `ai-hub/sources/`.\n- **Agent:** Sonnet at medium effort, a subagent in its own worktree of this repo.\n- **Cost:** 1.65 h, 170 model calls, 54M tokens read (context grew from 56k to 485k), about 6.5M\n  weighted; 106k tokens of visible output. About 4,270 lines written, 3,965 of them game code\n  inside the engine crates.\n- **Verdict (agent's):** the renderer, wasm shell, audio synth and headless tools carried the\n  visuals and the first wasm build ran; the gameplay half didn't help a non-RPG, non-physics game,\n  so 4,000 lines went into a game layer with no engine facility, and the packaging was all its own.\n- **Checked:** the claims about `vehicle.rs` and `health.rs` hold (rapier-bound; no weapons,\n  damage or fuel), and AGENTS.md now says so. The game didn't touch props, format 2 or the studios:\n  its units are SDF and cube parts drawn in code, because a prop can't be drawn from game state.\n- **Acted on:** the single-file web build (every test game needs one), the AGENTS.md wording, and\n  the asset plan's row 4.1 now includes drawing a library asset from game code. Everything else\n  waits for a second game.\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017N2dhBv5L5MH4zFLxdFSWf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
