{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ah1rt4V7c51s8qYQjVAYJK","type":"tool_result","content":"pav — Shardfall agent CLI\n\nUsage: pav <tool> [key=value ...] | pav repl [--stop-on-error] | pav live [addr] [--stop-on-error] | pav mcp [scene] | pav mcp --live [addr] | pav help\n\nTools:\n  scenes     List built-in scenes.  \n  load       Start a fresh simulation of a scene.  scene=<string> seed=<integer>\n  step       Advance the simulation N ticks as fast as possible.  ticks=<integer>\n  status     Tick, time, entity/block counts and state hash.  \n  entities   List entities (id, name, position).  name=<string>\n  params     List tunable parameters (sim.*, camera.*, view.*) with values and ranges.  prefix=<string>\n  set        Set a parameter: path=value.  path=<string> value=<string>\n  camera     Apply a camera preset (no args lists them).  preset=<string>\n  capture    Render a screenshot (PNG) with the software/real GPU.  out=<string> width=<integer> height=<integer> stats=<string> ui=<boolean>\n  bench      Measure simulation ticks per second.  ticks=<integer>\n  gpu        Describe the GPU adapter used for captures.  \n  player     Player state: feet position, velocity, grounded, posture, climbing.  \n  input      Drive the player: hold a move direction/buttons for N ticks (press = only on the first tick).  move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> ticks=<integer>\n  spawn      Spawn a prop.  shape=<string> size=<array> pos=<array> color=<string> body=<string> name=<string>\n  despawn    Remove an entity.  id=<integer>\n  teleport   Move an entity (default: the player; for characters pos = feet).  id=<integer> pos=<array>\n  rewind     Go back in time: ticks=N back, or to tick=T. Starts a new timeline.  ticks=<integer> tick=<integer>\n  snapshot_save Save the full state to a file.  path=<string>\n  snapshot_load Load a state file.  path=<string>\n  record_save Save the inputs since the scene started as a replay file (JSON).  path=<string>\n  rooms      List rooms in the world (key, name, wing, bounds, entrance).  \n  room       Info card of a room (default: the one the player is in).  key=<string>\n  guide      The field guide: words the station guides use (term=, search=), or every room's ask-for-it phrases (asks=true).  term=<string> search=<string> asks=<boolean>\n  goto       Teleport the player into a room (room=key), to the plaza (room=hub) or to a position.  room=<string> pos=<array>\n  room_reset Rebuild a room from its definition (default: current room).  key=<string>\n  room_check Validate a room file without loading it. Returns errors with line/column.  path=<string>\n  room_reload Re-read room files from the rooms directory and rebuild changed rooms (hot reload).  \n  stream     Streaming state: active/dormant regions. point=[x,y,z] adds an interest point, clear=true removes them.  point=<array> clear=<boolean>\n  filmstrip  Capture N frames, `every` ticks apart (optionally driving the player), tiled into one PNG.  frames=<integer> every=<integer> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> out=<string>\n  camera_bench Render the current moment from several camera setups, tiled into one PNG.  presets=<string> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> out=<string>\n  npcs       Non-player characters and creatures: body plan, feet, velocity, brain, steps taken, flinch.  name=<string>\n  signal     Send a pad signal (spawners listening for it fire on the next tick), then step 1 tick.  name=<string>\n  course     Course state: current run (timer, gates, hits, falls), last result, best times, checkpoint.  \n  feel       Feel metrics of the player: response ticks, time to top speed, stopping, turnaround, last jump.  \n  audio_capture Run N ticks (optionally driving the player) and render the game's sounds to a .wav file.  ticks=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> out=<string>\n  replay     Rebuild the scene from a replay file, run all its inputs and verify the final state hash.  path=<string>\n  game       Shardfall status: the hero (level, life, gold, skills), monsters by family and rarity, the wave.  \n  hero       Change the hero: play as another character (character=KEY: game/heroes.toml; each keeps their own hero, the stash is shared), level, gold, xp to add, a skill on a bar slot (slot=0..5 skill=key), full heal.  character=<string> level=<integer> gold=<integer> xp=<number> slot=<integer> skill=<string> heal=<boolean>\n  monster    Spawn monsters of a family near the hero (or at pos). Lists families with no arguments.  family=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> count=<integer> pos=<array> aggro=<boolean>\n  play       A games/ game's HUD, outcome and status.  bot=<boolean> ticks=<integer> seeds=<integer>\n  autoplay   Let a bot play for N seconds (fight, skills, potions, dodge telegraphs); reports kills, deaths, damage taken, xp, gold.  seconds=<number> goal=<array>\n  skills     Every skill (hero and monster) with its numbers, from game/skills.toml.  key=<string>\n  game_reload Re-read the game data folder (./game or $PAV_GAME) for live editing; reports errors.  \n  loot_roll  Roll items without playing (item level, rarity, slot, count): full tooltips, or a summary of many rolls (rarity spread, affix frequency, value ranges) to check loot tables.  level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> count=<integer> bonus=<number> seed=<integer>\n  give       Give the hero an item: a unique by key, or a rolled item (level, rarity, slot); optionally wear it at once.  unique=<string> base=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> equip=<boolean>\n  inventory  The hero's worn gear, bag and stash with every item described, gold, and the vendor's wares in town.  brief=<boolean>\n  game_cmd   A menu action as the player does it (in the input frame: replays include it): pickup|equip|unequip|drop|sell|buy|stash|take|sell_all|bar|travel|use|auto_loot|sort|character with id/slot/skill/place/spot/name.  do=<string> id=<integer> slot=<string> skill=<string> place=<string> depth=<integer> spot=<integer> rarity=<integer> name=<string>\n  ui         The game UI as the player sees it: HUD, windows and touch controls as text; image=true draws it over the game.  open=<string> close=<string> device=<string> hover=<array> click=<array> width=<integer> height=<integer> image=<boolean> out=<string>\n  tree_map   Draw the passive tree (and the first Astral rings) to a PNG: sectors coloured, notables/keystones/masteries ringed, skill nodes blue-ringed, the hero's allocation highlighted.  size=<integer> rings=<integer> out=<string>\n  tree       The hero's passive tree: points, what the allocation gives; find nodes (find=fire or find=keystone), take=NAME allocates the shortest path to a node, refund=, respec=true, mastery=NAME option=N.  find=<string> take=<string> refund=<string> respec=<boolean> mastery=<string> option=<integer> astral=<boolean>\n  genome     Grow a creature from a seed (Spore-style genome: body, parts, palette, archetype, skills, name); body=/archetype=/element= fix those; spawn=true puts it in the game.  seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> spawn=<boolean>\n  bestiary   Generate many genomes and summarise the spread (bodies, archetypes, elements, parts, distinct names) with examples: checks the generator's variety.  count=<integer> seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string>\n  boss       List the designed bosses, or spawn one (key=hollow_king) or a generated one (seed=N) near the hero.  key=<string> seed=<integer> level=<integer>\n  turntable  Render a creature alone from several angles into one PNG: seed= (genome, with body/archetype/element), family=, boss=, character=, or the hero; def= lays JSON puppet fields over it. Reports its anatomy.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> def=<object> angles=<integer> size=<integer> out=<string>\n  animsheet  Render a creature (default: the hero) acting, frame by frame, into one PNG: skill= (swing= a combo's later swing), move= (anim/moves.toml) or clip=; def={\"figure\":NAME} draws an imported body.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> skill=<string> swing=<integer> move=<string> hit=<number> side=<number> clip=<string> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> def=<object> frames=<integer> tilt=<number> size=<integer> out=<string>\n\n{\"cols\":\"seed outcome seconds\",\"game\":\"starter\",\"not_won\":[],\"runs\":[[1,\"won\",17.12],[2,\"won\",17.23],[3,\"won\",14.57]],\"wins\":\"3/3\"}\n\nreal\t0m0.370s\nuser\t0m0.359s\nsys\t0m0.013s\n{\"height\":540,\"path\":\"../spike-out/starter.png\",\"render_ms\":757,\"tick\":120,\"width\":960}\n{\"height\":540,\"path\":\"../spike-out/world.png\",\"render_ms\":896,\"tick\":60,\"width\":960}\nstarter.png\nworld.png\n_template.toml\naction_moves.toml\nbloom.toml\nbullet_hell.toml\ncamera_bench.toml\ncatalogue.toml\nchains.toml\nclip_browser.toml\nconveyors.toml\ncreatures.toml\ndestruction.toml\ndistortion.toml\ndrift.toml\nfeel_lab.toml\nfilter_bench.toml\nfilters.toml\ngauntlet.toml\ngi.toml\nhelicopter.toml\nlibrary_hall.toml\nlight_shafts.toml\nlights.toml\nlimits.toml\nmaterials.toml\nmix_match.toml\nmotion_library.toml\npaint_print.toml\nparticles.toml\nplayground.toml\nrecoil.toml\nsandbox.toml\nsecondary.toml\nslalom.toml\nsoft_bodies.toml\nsquash.toml\nstacking.toml\nstealth.toml\nstore_showcase.toml\nstress.toml\nstyle_bench.toml\nstyles.toml\ntightrope.toml\ntiming_gates.toml\ntower.toml\ntransitions.toml\nwalk_cycles.toml\nwalk_styles.toml\nwind_water.toml","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3d8a44-de88-4121-ac6f-adf7ca0c1ca2","uuid":"f1cfe983-ad2b-4245-bb18-8abe6602ce0f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:26:02.659Z","too