{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC4viAz31mR2sf5R91r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S6TvBBcdBxzoEThAdhFeqJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md')\ns = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    c = s.count(a)\n    assert c >= 1 and (n == 0 or c == n), (a[:70], c)\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# Introit is the waltz: one time signature everywhere.\nrep(\"**Introit** (4/4), **Lacrimosa** (6/8)\", \"**Introit** (3/4), **Lacrimosa** (6/8)\")\nrep(\"The ECG goes into 4/4 time. The Hush wakes under pressure\", \"The ECG goes into 3/4 time. The Hush wakes under pressure\")\nrep(\"> **Teddy:** Guys? The ECG just went into four-four time. Hearts aren't in a time signature. Hearts aren't *allowed*.\",\n    \"> **Teddy:** Guys? The ECG just went into three-four time. That's a waltz. Hearts aren't in a time signature. Hearts aren't *allowed*.\")\nrep(\"**Introit, 4/4.** A violet nodule moves under the tissue, seen as a bump. Every 4 beats it steps\\nsomewhere new (a ripple telegraphs on beat 3)\",\n    \"**Introit, 3/4.** A violet nodule moves under the tissue, seen as a bump. Every 3 beats it steps\\nsomewhere new (a ripple telegraphs on beat 2)\")\nrep(\"a motif\\n  per strain in its own meter (4/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8)\", \"a motif\\n  per strain in its own meter (3/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8)\")\n\n# Appendix reference.\nrep(\"a JS shim (Appendix C) owns every `AIHub` call\", \"a JS shim (Appendix B) owns every `AIHub` call\")\n\n# The ring in Case 7.\nrep(\"Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7). Up-left: IV Push.\",\n    \"Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\")\n\n# Scripted Codes.\nrep(\"Success returns vitals to 30. Resident gets 2 per case, Attending 1, Chief 0. Otherwise the patient\\ndies. Time running out is also death.\",\n    \"Success returns vitals to 30. Resident gets 2 per case, Attending 1, Chief 0 (the scripted stops in Cases\\n2 and 7 don't count). Otherwise the patient dies. Time running out is also death.\")\n\n# Camera detail.\nrep(\"- Camera: tilt 73°, distance 19.9, fov 36°, follow lag 0, target (0, 0, 0.2).\",\n    \"- Camera: tilt 73°, yaw 0, distance 19.9, fov 36°, follow lag 0, height offset 0, target (0, 0, 0.2).\")\n\n# Hub details.\nrep(\"`hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (keep the patient alive; top score leads the team), `hub:session-howto`.\",\n    \"`hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (under 60 characters: keep the patient alive), `hub:session-howto` (under 80).\")\nrep(\"**passed the harness in all required runs**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50,\\n  loss 5; `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\",\n    \"**passed the harness in every run**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5;\\n  `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; `players=1`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\")\nrep(\"Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at 20 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\\n  edges repeated until seen.\",\n    \"Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\\n  edges repeated until seen.\")\nrep(\"Stay under 20 messages a second. Predict locally\", \"Each copy may send at most 20 messages a second. Predict locally\")\n\n# 10-foot canvas: precise.\nrep(\"Lay out every screen on a virtual 1920×1080 canvas (`ctx.set_zoom_factor(h/1080)` in\\negui).\",\n    \"Lay out every screen on a virtual 1920×1080 canvas: set egui's zoom so the screen is\\n1080 points tall (`zoom = height_px / 1080 / scale_factor`, in the app and in the headless UI alike).\")\n\n# Hover in the world.\nrep(\"All click targets are real: menu items, instruments on the tray, the \\\"advance\\\" area in\\nstory scenes.\",\n    \"All click targets are real: menu items, instruments on the tray, the \\\"advance\\\" area in\\nstory scenes. In operations, hovering a valid target highlights it.\")\n\n# The bot, and the card scene.\nrep(\"Scene\\nnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/mirror`.\",\n    \"Scene\\nnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/card`,\\n`surgery/mirror` (✔ the engine passes everything after the first `/` to your `build`).\")\nrep(\"Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\\nreal-time.\",\n    \"Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\\nreal-time.\\n\\n**The bot** (`Game::bot`, one implementation) is a task planner: it picks the most urgent valid task, selects the tool, moves\\nat a human cursor speed and performs the gesture, with noise scaled by `bot_skill`. It drives the tests, the balance tool,\\nattract mode, the Case 7 partner and the Echo's ghost hands. Teach it each rule as you add the rule.\")\n\n# Player removal is tested.\nrep(\"`build_standalone_room` always spawns a player, so in `build` despawn it and set\\n   `sim.state.player = None`. The level file holds\",\n    \"`build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it. The level file holds\")\nrep(\"`sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target and the game can set it.\", \"`sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target.\")\n\n# HUD lines.\nrep(\"8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD.\",\n    \"8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\")\n\n# Packer note.\nrep(\"The script already checks that the page holds nothing that would close an inline script early; keep that check for the shim too.\",\n    \"The packer already refuses JS glue holding `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`; apply the same check to the client and the shim. ✔ `session.js` holds none.\")\n\n# Shim: the remaining calls.\nrep(\"  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\\n\",\n    \"  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\\n\"\n    \"  H.answer = (what) => AIHub.answer(what);                                           // the card: 'ready' or 'more'\\n\"\n    \"  H.time = () => AIHub.time();\\n\"\n    \"  H.finish = (json) => AIHub.finish(JSON.parse(json));                               // host, at the round's end\\n\")\n\n# House rules.\nrep(\"Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` (short), plus \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\",\n    \"Stay inside your dev folder: other agents build beside you. Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`\\n(short), plus \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\")\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\nprint('edits applied')\nEOF\nwc -w PLAN.md; grep -n -i \"exit-interview\\.\\|GameTitle\\|\\.html\\b\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-110; echo '--- source names (should appear only in the research note):'; grep -n -i \"derek\\|naomi\\|stiles\\|caduceus\\|hope hospital\\|guilt\\|delphi\\|healing touch\\|kyriaki\\|angie\\|trauma center\\|under the knife\\|new blood\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120; echo '--- sections:'; grep -n \"^## \\|^### \" PLAN.md | cut -c1-70","description":"Apply corrections and check the plan for names it must leave out"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":467888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1690},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3d8a44-de88-4121-ac6f-adf7ca0c1ca2","uuid":"d1a92853-75a9-4076-81c7-d33e36a9f454","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:00:41.238Z","request_id":"req_011CgjC4vRK5zs6uDKyRxLWE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S6TvBBcdBxzoEThAdhFeqJ":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211911__x2c3ab6/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md')\ns = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    c = s.count(a)\n    assert c >= 1 and (n == 0 or c == n), (a[:70], c)\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# Introit is the waltz: one time signature everywhere.\nrep(\"**Introit** (4/4), **Lacrimosa** (6/8)\", \"**Introit** (3/4), **Lacrimosa** (6/8)\")\nrep(\"The ECG goes into 4/4 time. The Hush wakes under pressure\", \"The ECG goes into 3/4 time. The Hush wakes under pressure\")\nrep(\"> **Teddy:** Guys? The ECG just went into four-four time. Hearts aren't in a time signature. Hearts aren't *allowed*.\",\n    \"> **Teddy:** Guys? The ECG just went into three-four time. That's a waltz. Hearts aren't in a time signature. Hearts aren't *allowed*.\")\nrep(\"**Introit, 4/4.** A violet nodule moves under the tissue, seen as a bump. Every 4 beats it steps\\nsomewhere new (a ripple telegraphs on beat 3)\",\n    \"**Introit, 3/4.** A violet nodule moves under the tissue, seen as a bump. Every 3 beats it steps\\nsomewhere new (a ripple telegraphs on beat 2)\")\nrep(\"a motif\\n  per strain in its own meter (4/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8)\", \"a motif\\n  per strain in its own meter (3/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8)\")\n\n# Appendix reference.\nrep(\"a JS shim (Appendix C) owns every `AIHub` call\", \"a JS shim (Appendix B) owns every `AIHub` call\")\n\n# The ring in Case 7.\nrep(\"Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7). Up-left: IV Push.\",\n    \"Left: Scanner (Cryoprobe in\\nCase 7, where the nodules stay visible). Up-left: IV Push.\")\n\n# Scripted Codes.\nrep(\"Success returns vitals to 30. Resident gets 2 per case, Attending 1, Chief 0. Otherwise the patient\\ndies. Time running out is also death.\",\n    \"Success returns vitals to 30. Resident gets 2 per case, Attending 1, Chief 0 (the scripted stops in Cases\\n2 and 7 don't count). Otherwise the patient dies. Time running out is also death.\")\n\n# Camera detail.\nrep(\"- Camera: tilt 73°, distance 19.9, fov 36°, follow lag 0, target (0, 0, 0.2).\",\n    \"- Camera: tilt 73°, yaw 0, distance 19.9, fov 36°, follow lag 0, height offset 0, target (0, 0, 0.2).\")\n\n# Hub details.\nrep(\"`hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (keep the patient alive; top score leads the team), `hub:session-howto`.\",\n    \"`hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (under 60 characters: keep the patient alive), `hub:session-howto` (under 80).\")\nrep(\"**passed the harness in all required runs**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50,\\n  loss 5; `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\",\n    \"**passed the harness in every run**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5;\\n  `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; `players=1`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\")\nrep(\"Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at 20 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\\n  edges repeated until seen.\",\n    \"Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\\n  edges repeated until seen.\")\nrep(\"Stay under 20 messages a second. Predict locally\", \"Each copy may send at most 20 messages a second. Predict locally\")\n\n# 10-foot canvas: precise.\nrep(\"Lay out every screen on a virtual 1920×1080 canvas (`ctx.set_zoom_factor(h/1080)` in\\negui).\",\n    \"Lay out every screen on a virtual 1920×1080 canvas: set egui's zoom so the screen is\\n1080 points tall (`zoom = height_px / 1080 / scale_factor`, in the app and in the headless UI alike).\")\n\n# Hover in the world.\nrep(\"All click targets are real: menu items, instruments on the tray, the \\\"advance\\\" area in\\nstory scenes.\",\n    \"All click targets are real: menu items, instruments on the tray, the \\\"advance\\\" area in\\nstory scenes. In operations, hovering a valid target highlights it.\")\n\n# The bot, and the card scene.\nrep(\"Scene\\nnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/mirror`.\",\n    \"Scene\\nnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/card`,\\n`surgery/mirror` (✔ the engine passes everything after the first `/` to your `build`).\")\nrep(\"Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\\nreal-time.\",\n    \"Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\\nreal-time.\\n\\n**The bot** (`Game::bot`, one implementation) is a task planner: it picks the most urgent valid task, selects the tool, moves\\nat a human cursor speed and performs the gesture, with noise scaled by `bot_skill`. It drives the tests, the balance tool,\\nattract mode, the Case 7 partner and the Echo's ghost hands. Teach it each rule as you add the rule.\")\n\n# Player removal is tested.\nrep(\"`build_standalone_room` always spawns a player, so in `build` despawn it and set\\n   `sim.state.player = None`. The level file holds\",\n    \"`build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it. The level file holds\")\nrep(\"`sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target and the game can set it.\", \"`sim.state.focus`\\n   is the camera target.\")\n\n# HUD lines.\nrep(\"8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD.\",\n    \"8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\")\n\n# Packer note.\nrep(\"The script already checks that the page holds nothing that would close an inline script early; keep that check for the shim too.\",\n    \"The packer already refuses JS glue holding `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`; apply the same check to the client and the shim. ✔ `session.js` holds none.\")\n\n# Shim: the remaining calls.\nrep(\"  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\\n\",\n    \"  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\\n\"\n    \"  H.answer = (what) => AIHub.answer(what);                                           // the card: 'ready' or 'more'\\n\"\n    \"  H.time = () => AIHub.time();\\n\"\n    \"  H.finish = (json) => AIHub.finish(JSON.parse(json));                               // host, at the round's end\\n\")\n\n# House rules.\nrep(\"Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` (short), plus \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\",\n    \"Stay inside your dev folder: other agents build beside you. Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`\\n(short), plus \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\")\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\nprint('edits applied')\nEOF\nwc -w PLAN.md; grep -n -i \"exit-interview\\.\\|GameTitle\\|\\.html\\b\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-110; echo '--- source names (should appear only in the research note):'; grep -n -i \"derek\\|naomi\\|stiles\\|caduceus\\|hope hospital\\|guilt\\|delphi\\|healing touch\\|kyriaki\\|angie\\|trauma center\\|under the knife\\|new blood\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120; echo '--- sections:'; grep -n \"^## \\|^### \" PLAN.md | cut -c1-70","description":"Apply corrections and check the plan for names it must leave out"}}}
